<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Theoretical proof of NoLan-Plus</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The core mechanism of NoLan-Plus is a dynamic weighting method that uses KL divergence to measure the difference between multimodal and text-only output distributions.
In addition to the empirical justification and experimental research for using KL divergence, we conduct the following theoretical analysis.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition of Visual Object Hallucination.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Visual Object Hallucination is defined as the case where the model’s response <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> is almost independent of the visual input <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> given a textual prompt <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. Formally, this dependency is quantified using the conditional mutual information:</p>
<table id="A1.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(y;v\mid x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(y;v\mid x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">A lower mutual information implies stronger hallucination. As an extreme case, if <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> are independent, then the response is generated without reference to the visual input, and</p>
<table id="A1.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(y;v\mid x)=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(y;v\mid x)=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Connecting Conditional Mutual Information to KL Divergence.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">For a fixed prompt <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="A1.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{m}(y)=P_{\theta}(y\mid v,x),\quad p_{u}(y)=P_{\theta}(y\mid x)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{m}(y)=P_{\theta}(y\mid v,x),\quad p_{u}(y)=P_{\theta}(y\mid x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is the output distribution conditioned on both image and text, and <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> is conditioned on text only.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">By the standard identity between conditional mutual information and KL divergence, we have:</p>
<table id="A1.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="I(y;v\mid x)=\mathbb{E}_{v\mid x}\Big[D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\big(p_{m}\,\|\,p_{u}\big)\Big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(y;v\mid x)=\mathbb{E}_{v\mid x}\Big[D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\big(p_{m}\,\|\,p_{u}\big)\Big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Starting from the definition of conditional mutual information:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(y;v\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(y;v\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{v,y\mid x}\left[\log\frac{P(y,v\mid x)}{P(y\mid x)P(v\mid x)}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{v,y\mid x}\left[\log\frac{P(y,v\mid x)}{P(y\mid x)P(v\mid x)}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{v,y\mid x}\left[\log\frac{P(y\mid v,x)}{P(y\mid x)}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{v,y\mid x}\left[\log\frac{P(y\mid v,x)}{P(y\mid x)}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{v\mid x}\left[\sum_{y}P(y\mid v,x)\log\frac{P(y\mid v,x)}{P(y\mid x)}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>y</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{v\mid x}\left[\sum_{y}P(y\mid v,x)\log\frac{P(y\mid v,x)}{P(y\mid x)}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{v\mid x}\left[D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\big(P(Y\mid v,x)\,\|\,P(Y\mid x)\big)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{v\mid x}\left[D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\big(P(Y\mid v,x)\,\|\,P(Y\mid x)\big)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{v\mid x}\left[D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\big(p_{m}\,\|\,p_{u}\big)\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{v\mid x}\left[D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\big(p_{m}\,\|\,p_{u}\big)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, a lower KL divergence <math id="A1.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{KL}}(p_{m}\,\|\,p_{u})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{KL}}(p_{m}\,\|\,p_{u})</annotation></semantics></math> indicates a lower mutual information between the visual input and the response, leading to stronger hallucination.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Uncertainty analysis and language prior suppression</h3>

<figure id="A1.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A1.T6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 6</span>: </span><span id="A1.T6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Entropy-based uncertainty evaluation across four benchmarks: POPE, MME, MM-Vet, and LLaVA-Bench. Results indicate that NoLan achieves the lowest uncertainty in all settings.</span></figcaption>
<div id="A1.T6.5" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:207.0pt;height:49.7pt;vertical-align:-23.3pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-48.9pt,11.7pt) scale(0.679313722431731,0.679313722431731) ;">
<table id="A1.T6.5.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A1.T6.5.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T6.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><span id="A1.T6.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Decoding</span></td>
<td id="A1.T6.5.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="A1.T6.5.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">POPE<span id="A1.T6.5.1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <math id="A1.T6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></td>
<td id="A1.T6.5.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="A1.T6.5.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">MME<span id="A1.T6.5.1.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <math id="A1.T6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></td>
